{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>But if you would hear me.</b> You tell me to heed you and take it for nothing — I am unable to do so." "<b>But if you would hear me.</b> Would that you heed me." "<b>I have given.</b> דני\"ש בְּלַעַ\"ז — it is ready by me, and would that I had already given it to you."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {2 "The la'az is Old French ge l' ai donné or equivalent, 'I have given it'; Rashi reads the perfect נתתי as effectively present-ready."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:04.068524302Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}